WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.672
This lesson follows the instructional themes of school 5B. Our original scene and reflection tasks prepare the same skills without reproducing the school competency check. Scene management is clinical work: uncontrolled hazards can prevent care and create additional patients.
本课依学校5B教学主题展开，以原创现场及反思任务准备相同技能，不复制学校能力考核。现场管理属于临床工作：未控制危险会妨碍照护，并可能造成更多伤员。

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:31.992
The sequence is not one safety check followed by a fixed checklist. Risk changes from dispatch through approach, contact, care, movement and transfer; reassessment belongs in every phase.
这不是一次安全检查后就照固定清单行动。风险会从派遣、接近、接触、照护、搬动到交接持续变化；每一阶段都需要复评。

00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:42.696
We will use a fresh multi-vehicle scene to practise the school frameworks. The case is original and does not reproduce the older companion lesson or a school assessment answer.
我们会用一个全新的多车辆现场练习学校框架。案例为原创，不照搬旧补充网站课程或学校考核答案。

00:00:42.696 --> 00:01:00.264
Operational risk assessment means noticing a hazard, considering who could be harmed and deciding what is safe enough to do next. It is repeated, not completed once at the curb. Infection-control point-of-care risk assessment is a related but more specific exposure decision.
行动风险评估是发现危险、考虑谁可能受伤，并决定下一步是否安全；它需要反复进行，不能在路边完成一次就算结束。感染控制中的床旁风险评估与此相连，但更具体地针对暴露作判断。

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:13.104
A short verbal estimate can be practical: what can happen, how soon, who is in the exposure path, and which reliable control would reduce the risk. A numerical score never grants permission to enter.
简短口头判断可以很实用：可能发生什么、多久会发生、谁处于暴露路径，以及哪种可靠控制能降低风险。风险分数本身从不构成进入许可。

00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:27.168
If there is an uncontrolled threat, the correct clinical move may be to stop, increase distance, reposition, withdraw or wait for a qualified specialist. That pause protects the ability to return and provide care.
若危险尚未控制，正确的临床行动可能是停止、拉开距离、改位、撤离，或等待合格专业人员。暂停能保护救援人员，使其之后仍可返回照护。

00:01:27.168 --> 00:01:44.280
Operational risk assessment covers traffic, unstable structures, violence, machinery, weather and the work itself. In infection control, point-of-care risk assessment more specifically considers infectious exposure during a particular patient interaction.
行动风险评估涵盖交通、不稳定结构、暴力、机械、天气及工作任务。感染控制中的床旁风险评估，则更具体地考虑某次患者接触中的感染暴露。

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:56.976
These are connected questions, not interchangeable labels. A mask decision does not clear a traffic hazard; moving to a safer road position does not decide whether suctioning could expose your face.
两者相连，却不是可互换标签。选择口罩不能解决交通危险；移到更安全道路位置，也不能决定吸引操作是否会使面部暴露。

00:01:56.976 --> 00:02:11.712
Prefer controls that reduce exposure before relying only on personal protective equipment. A controlled access route, assigned traffic management and a prepared clean work area can prevent hazards that gloves cannot stop.
应先用减少暴露的控制措施，而不是只靠个人防护装备。受控通道、指定交通管理及准备好的洁净工作区，能预防手套无法阻挡的危险。

00:02:11.712 --> 00:02:23.616
Say the decision aloud: the hazard, who is exposed, the control and what would make you stop. Revisit it when the patient, procedure, environment or available protection changes.
口头说明危险、暴露者、控制措施及停下来的触发条件。患者、操作、环境或可用防护改变时，重新评估。

00:02:23.616 --> 00:02:39.984
A 360-degree survey deliberately looks beyond the patient and the first obvious mechanism. Observe approach and exit routes, overhead loads, ground stability, power sources, smoke direction, weather and where other people are moving.
360度环视要求把视野扩展到患者及显见伤因之外。观察接近与撤离路线、头顶重物、地面稳定性、电源、烟气方向、天气和人群流动。

00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:53.760
Different hazard families can combine. A vehicle collision may include traffic, leaking fuel, damaged power lines, agitated bystanders and a changing wind that carries vapour toward the staging area.
不同危险类型可能叠加。车辆碰撞可同时涉及交通、燃油泄漏、受损电线、激动旁观者，以及把蒸气吹向集结区的风向变化。

00:02:53.760 --> 00:03:03.600
The survey is not a guarantee that the scene is safe. It creates a working picture that must be updated whenever the scene, task or patient condition changes.
环视并不保证现场绝对安全；它形成一个暂定态势图，每当现场、任务或患者状态变化时都必须更新。

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:17.280
METHANE organizes an early report: Major incident declared, Exact location, Type of incident, Hazards, Access, Number and type of casualties, and Emergency services required or present.
METHANE用于组织早期报告：是否宣布重大事件、准确位置、事件类型、危险、通道、伤员数量与类型，以及所需或已到场的紧急服务。

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:29.640
A useful report is concise and updateable. State what you know, label estimates as estimates, identify the main hazard and describe the access or staging issue that changes responder safety.
有效报告应简洁并便于更新。只报告已知信息，把估算标为估算，指出主要危险，并说明影响救援安全的通道或集结问题。

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:39.768
Do not delay an initial warning while trying to complete every field perfectly. Give the critical known facts, then update command as information improves.
不要为了把每个栏位填得完美而延迟初次警报。先传递关键已知事实，信息完善后再向指挥更新。

00:03:39.768 --> 00:03:57.528
Here is an original report: Control, Unit Seventy-Two, possible major incident at Ridgeway depot west gate. A canopy has collapsed. Stability and power status are not confirmed. Hold incoming crews at the west access point.
这是一份原创报告：“调度，72车，Ridgeway场站西门可能发生重大事件。顶棚已坍塌，稳定性与电力状态未确认。请让后续人员在西侧接近点等候。”

00:03:57.528 --> 00:04:11.208
Continue: Seven patients are visible from our position; that count is provisional. Request fire assistance and additional ambulances. We will update the safe access route after scene control is confirmed.
继续：“从当前位置可见7名患者，数量为暂估。请求消防及更多救护车。现场控制确认后，我们会更新安全接近路线。”

00:04:11.208 --> 00:04:23.904
The report names uncertainty instead of disguising it as certainty. Do not announce that the area is safe because you cannot see smoke, or silently turn a visible count into a complete casualty count.
这份报告明确不确定性，而不是把它伪装成确定。不能因为看不见烟就宣布安全，也不能把可见人数默认为全部伤员人数。

00:04:23.904 --> 00:04:36.936
A later update might change the count or close an access route. Identify the change and obtain acknowledgment for a critical restriction. The shared incident picture must change when the evidence changes.
后续更新可能改变人数或关闭通道。应指出变化，并对关键限制取得确认。证据改变时，共同事件态势也必须改变。

00:04:36.936 --> 00:04:47.952
Reassess after wind shifts, fire or traffic changes, a load moves, a new patient appears, a bystander becomes threatening or protective equipment is damaged.
风向变化、火势或交通改变、重物移动、新伤员出现、旁观者变得有威胁，或防护装备受损后，都要重新评估。

00:04:47.952 --> 00:04:58.200
Before movement, verify that the route, people and equipment still support a safe transfer. A safe approach does not prove that the egress route is safe.
搬动前要再次核实路线、人员和设备是否仍支持安全转移。接近路线安全，不代表撤离路线也安全。

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:10.848
If the risk picture becomes unacceptable, stop work and report the reason. A useful stop-work message names the hazard, its location, who is exposed and what support or control is needed.
若风险变得不可接受，应停工并说明原因。有效的停工报告要指出危险、位置、暴露者及所需支援或控制措施。

00:05:10.848 --> 00:05:24.504
An incident management system creates a shared structure for command, operations, planning, logistics and information. A small incident may combine roles; a larger event separates them as needed.
事件管理系统为指挥、行动、计划、后勤及信息建立共同架构。小事件可以合并职责；规模扩大时则应按需拆分。

00:05:24.504 --> 00:05:36.840
The system reduces duplicated work and conflicting instructions. Personnel should know who supervises them, what task they own, where they report and how urgent changes will be communicated.
该系统可减少重复工作及互相冲突的指令。每人都应知道直属负责人、自己的任务、报告地点，以及如何传递紧急变化。

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:56.544
Use the current BC incident structure and dispatch procedures. First-arriving responsibilities include initial command and triage functions; a later arrival or higher clinical rank does not automatically transfer those roles. Establish, communicate and hand over the assignment explicitly.
应使用BC现行事件架构及派遣流程。先到人员职责包括初始指挥与检伤职能；后到场或临床职级较高，不会自动转移这些角色。应明确建立、沟通及交接任务。

00:05:56.544 --> 00:06:10.464
The current BCEHS MCI page divides first-arriving responsibilities into Incident Commander and Triage Leader functions. The initial command function collects the scene picture and communicates with the communication centre.
现行BCEHS多伤员页面把先到人员职责分为事件指挥与检伤领导职能。初始指挥职能负责收集现场态势，并与通信中心联系。

00:06:10.464 --> 00:06:23.616
This is not the same as inventing an independent command system. Establish the appropriate initial organization under the service plan, identify yourself clearly and request the resources the scene needs.
这不等于自行发明独立指挥系统。应按机构计划建立适当初始组织，清楚说明身份，并请求现场所需资源。

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:36.912
The initial command and triage roles remain in place unless appropriately relieved. A later arrival or higher clinical qualification does not, by itself, tell everyone that command has changed.
初始指挥与检伤角色会持续，直到适当人员明确接替。后到场或临床资格较高，本身并不表示所有人都已知道指挥发生改变。

00:06:36.912 --> 00:06:51.696
Use the deliberate transfer already taught: situation, hazards, objectives, resources, unresolved problems and acceptance. Tell affected crews who now holds the role and which instructions have changed.
应进行已经学习的明确交接：情况、危险、目标、资源、未解决问题及接任确认。告诉相关人员当前负责人及哪些指令已改变。

00:06:51.696 --> 00:07:07.656
A triage lead organizes rapid sorting and reports the emerging patient picture. A treatment lead organizes care after that first sort. Confusing these jobs can leave everyone treating one patient while other patients remain unseen.
检伤负责人组织快速分流，并报告不断完善的伤员态势。治疗负责人组织初筛后的照护。混淆职责可能使所有人都治疗一名患者，而其他患者尚无人查看。

00:07:07.656 --> 00:07:22.224
Transport coordination links patient priority, available crews and receiving capacity. Staging keeps arriving units available and accounted for instead of allowing each unit to choose its own patient or destination.
转运协调把患者优先级、可用人员与接收能力连接起来。集结管理使到场车辆保持可用并有记录，而不是各车自行挑患者或目的地。

00:07:22.224 --> 00:07:35.664
A scribe preserves important times, counts, assignments and updates. Small incidents may combine functions, but the team still needs to know who owns each decision and where information must go.
记录员保存重要时间、人数、任务分派及更新。小事件可合并职能，但团队仍须知道每项决定由谁负责、信息应传给谁。

00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:49.176
Closed-loop tasking means the recipient repeats the critical assignment and reports completion or a problem. Saying that someone should arrange transport is weaker than assigning the task to a named role and confirming it.
闭环任务沟通是接收者复述关键任务，再报告完成或遇到的问题。“应该有人安排转运”，不如明确交给某个角色并取得确认。

00:07:49.176 --> 00:08:01.848
A transfer of command is a deliberate handoff, not an assumption. The outgoing lead gives the current situation, hazards, objectives, resources, decisions and unresolved risks.
指挥交接必须明确进行，不能靠默认。原负责人要交代当前情况、危险、目标、资源、已作决定及尚未解决的风险。

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:12.504
The incoming lead confirms acceptance and states immediate priorities. Crews need to know the new command point and whether assignments or restricted areas have changed.
接任负责人要确认接任并说明眼前优先事项。各组必须知道新的指挥点，以及任务或限制区域是否改变。

00:08:12.504 --> 00:08:24.912
Use plain language and read-back for critical instructions. When a communication fails or a hazard changes, correct the shared picture promptly rather than assuming everyone heard the first message.
关键指令要用明语并复诵确认。通信失败或危险改变时，应及时修正共同态势，而不是假设所有人都听到了最初通报。

00:08:24.912 --> 00:08:36.336
Routine infection-prevention measures begin with hand hygiene and a point-of-care risk assessment. Add precautions according to the likely transmission route and current local policy.
常规感染预防从手卫生和现场风险评估开始。应依可能传播途径及现行当地政策增加防护。

00:08:36.336 --> 00:08:48.816
PPE must match both the hazard and the task. Gloves do not replace eye protection when splash is likely; a surgical mask does not protect against an unknown airborne chemical atmosphere.
防护装备必须同时匹配危险和任务。有飞溅风险时，手套不能替代眼部防护；医用外科口罩也不能保护人免受未知化学气体危害。

00:08:48.816 --> 00:09:01.584
Use the taught donning, removal, disposal and hand-hygiene sequence. If equipment is damaged, contaminated or outside your training, withdraw and follow the supervisor’s plan.
按受教的穿脱、弃置及手卫生顺序操作。若装备受损、污染或超出训练范围，应撤离并遵循负责人的计划。

00:09:01.584 --> 00:09:18.792
The school groups standard, contact, droplet and airborne precautions together. In Canadian terminology, routine practices apply to every patient; contact, droplet and airborne precautions are additional layers, sometimes used together.
学校把标准、接触、飞沫与空气传播防护放在一起介绍。加拿大术语中，常规措施适用于每位患者；接触、飞沫及空气传播防护属于额外层次，有时需要联合使用。

00:09:18.792 --> 00:09:35.544
Routine practice does not mean gloves for every possible touch. Select gloves for the expected task and exposure, including blood, body fluids, mucous membranes, non-intact skin or contaminated items, and follow local policy.
常规措施不表示任何接触都必须戴手套。应按任务及预期暴露选择，例如血液、体液、黏膜、破损皮肤或污染物品，并遵循本地政策。

00:09:35.544 --> 00:09:51.576
The transmission concern changes which barriers and environmental controls are needed. A coughing patient may need source control and additional protection; one symptom does not let you invent a diagnosis or ignore current pathogen-specific direction.
传播风险影响所需屏障与环境控制。咳嗽患者可能需要源头控制及额外防护；单一症状不能让你自行确诊，或忽视现行病原体专门指引。

00:09:51.576 --> 00:10:04.608
Hand hygiene, equipment cleaning and clean-to-dirty task organization still matter under every layer. More PPE cannot repair contaminated technique or an uncontrolled chemical atmosphere.
每个层次都仍需手卫生、设备清洁及由洁到污的任务安排。更多PPE不能弥补污染操作，也不能解决未控制化学气体环境。

00:10:04.608 --> 00:10:16.272
First choose the equipment for the task and check its condition. Plan where it will be removed and discarded. Clean your hands before beginning; gloves are not a replacement for that step.
先按任务选装备并检查状态，规划脱除及弃置位置。开始前清洁双手；手套不能替代这一步。

00:10:16.272 --> 00:10:33.600
The PHAC Appendix Ten example then uses gown, mask or respirator, eye protection and gloves. When a gown is required, the gloves cover its cuffs. This is a named example, not a claim that every specialized ensemble uses one order.
PHAC附录十的示例随后依次为隔离衣、口罩或呼吸防护器、眼部防护及手套。需要隔离衣时，手套覆盖袖口。这是有出处的示例，并非所有特殊防护组合都采用同一顺序。

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:48.144
For a tight-fitting respirator, use the make, model and size selected through fit testing and perform the user seal check as taught. A face shield adds eye or splash protection; it does not replace respiratory protection.
紧密贴合式呼吸防护器应使用适合性测试所确定的品牌、型号及尺寸，并按培训进行佩戴密合检查。面屏增加眼部或飞溅防护，不能替代呼吸防护。

00:10:48.144 --> 00:11:01.680
Before approaching, check that the items work together and allow the intended task. If a seal or barrier is not adequate, resolve the problem before exposure rather than hoping the next layer will compensate.
接近前确认装备相互兼容，且能完成预定任务。密合或屏障不足时，应在暴露前解决，而不是指望下一层来弥补。

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:16.200
PPE removal can transfer contamination onto hands, clothing or the face. Prepare the waste or reprocessing route and remove items deliberately, avoiding unnecessary contact with contaminated fronts.
脱除PPE可把污染转到手、衣物或面部。先准备废物或再处理路线，再有意识地脱除，避免不必要接触污染正面。

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:31.776
The PHAC example removes gloves and gown, cleans hands, removes eye protection and then the mask or respirator, and cleans hands again. Handle straps, ties or the designated clean parts rather than the exposed front.
PHAC示例先脱手套和隔离衣、清洁双手，再脱眼部防护及口罩或呼吸防护器，最后再次清洁双手。应接触带子、系带或指定洁净部位，而非暴露正面。

00:11:31.776 --> 00:11:46.344
The saved school narrative orders some steps differently. Keep that source difference visible and use the complete current employer or station protocol for the actual ensemble and removal location. Do not create a hybrid order from memory.
学校存档叙述中部分步骤顺序不同。应保留这个来源差异，并为实际装备及脱除位置使用完整现行机构或站点流程。不能凭记忆拼成混合顺序。

00:11:46.344 --> 00:12:01.992
If you contaminate your hands during removal, stop and perform the indicated hand hygiene before continuing. Report a breach, manage the exposed equipment appropriately and seek the required exposure follow-up rather than silently carrying on.
脱除中若手被污染，应停下并进行所需手卫生，再继续。应报告破口、适当处理暴露设备，并按要求开展暴露随访，不能默默继续。

00:12:01.992 --> 00:12:14.952
A fit test selects and evaluates a specific respirator make, model and size on a person. A user seal check is performed when putting it on. Passing one does not eliminate the need for the other.
适合性测试是在个人身上选择并评估具体品牌、型号及尺寸。佩戴密合检查则在戴上时进行。通过其中一个，不代表不再需要另一个。

00:12:14.952 --> 00:12:29.352
Facial hair in the sealing area, a changed face shape, incompatible eyewear or a different model may interfere with protection. Report the issue and use the respiratory-protection programme instead of improvising a fit solution.
密封处毛发、脸型变化、不兼容眼镜或更换型号，都可能妨碍防护。应报告并按呼吸防护计划处理，而不是自行想办法凑合密合。

00:12:29.352 --> 00:12:40.320
The testing schedule comes from the applicable programme and jurisdiction. Do not turn a generic educational interval into a claim about the school or your employer’s current schedule.
测试周期应依适用计划及辖区要求。不能把一般教育资料中的间隔，直接当作学校或雇主当前周期。

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:53.592
A filtering medical respirator does not solve an unknown chemical gas exposure or a low-oxygen atmosphere. That is a different hazard assessment requiring the incident’s specialist protection and access plan.
过滤式医疗呼吸防护器不能解决未知化学气体暴露或缺氧环境。这属于不同危险评估，需依事件的专业防护及通行计划。

00:12:53.592 --> 00:13:07.560
WHMIS/GHS labels and Safety Data Sheets help identify a known product’s hazards, routes of exposure, storage and emergency information. Learn how to locate them through an authorized source.
WHMIS/GHS标签及安全数据表可帮助识别已知产品的危险、暴露途径、储存及应急信息。应学习如何通过授权渠道查找。

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:17.616
Do not approach a leaking container simply to read its label. Use information supplied by witnesses, shipping documents or incident command from a safe position.
不要为了读取标签而接近泄漏容器。应在安全位置利用目击者、运输文件或事件指挥提供的信息。

00:13:17.616 --> 00:13:32.496
Unknown concentration, oxygen deficiency or reactive mixtures cannot be made safe by ordinary medical PPE. Isolation, monitoring and decontamination are specialist functions under the incident plan.
普通医疗PPE无法解决浓度未知、缺氧或反应性混合物风险。隔离、监测和去污属于事件计划下的专业职责。

00:13:32.496 --> 00:13:46.704
A flame and a flame over a circle are not interchangeable. The flame identifies specified fire-related hazards; the flame over a circle indicates an oxidizer, which can intensify combustion.
火焰与圆圈上方火焰不能互换。火焰表示指定的火灾相关危险；圆圈上方火焰表示氧化剂，可加剧燃烧。

00:13:46.704 --> 00:14:01.056
A cylinder symbol warns of pressure-related hazards. An exploding-bomb symbol identifies specified severe reactive hazards. Neither symbol tells a medical crew that a damaged container is safe to touch or move.
气瓶图标警示压力相关危险；爆炸弹图标识别指定的严重反应性危险。两者都不表示医疗人员可安全触碰或移动受损容器。

00:14:01.056 --> 00:14:13.152
Corrosion can concern skin, eyes or metals according to the product classification. Do not assume that all corrosives have the same concentration, first aid or protective equipment.
腐蚀图标按产品分类可涉及皮肤、眼睛或金属。不能假设所有腐蚀品浓度、急救或防护装备都一样。

00:14:13.152 --> 00:14:24.144
The standard symbols shown here support visual recognition. The full label and Safety Data Sheet determine the product information; the incident plan determines what you may safely do.
这里的标准图形用于视觉识别。完整标签及安全数据表提供产品信息；事件计划决定你可以安全做什么。

00:14:24.144 --> 00:14:38.736
The skull and crossbones identifies specified severe acute toxicity. The exclamation mark covers other specified harmful or irritant effects. The difference does not mean that an exclamation-mark product is harmless.
骷髅交叉骨表示指定的严重急性毒性；感叹号涵盖其他指定的有害或刺激效应。两者不同，不表示感叹号产品无害。

00:14:38.736 --> 00:14:54.288
The human silhouette with a chest starburst identifies specified serious health hazards. Read the hazard statement to learn whether the concern is respiratory sensitization, organ toxicity, reproductive effects or another listed hazard.
胸部有星状标记的人形图标表示指定的严重健康危害。要读危险说明，判断涉及呼吸道致敏、器官毒性、生殖影响还是其他列出的危险。

00:14:54.288 --> 00:15:06.792
Canada’s biohazardous infectious materials symbol has a black circular border, not the usual red diamond. The environment symbol may appear but is not required by WHMIS.
加拿大生物危害感染性物质图标采用黑色圆边框，而不是常见红菱形。环境图标可能出现，但不是WHMIS必需项。

00:15:06.792 --> 00:15:21.624
Some hazardous classes do not require a pictogram at all. No symbol, a missing label or an unknown product is not evidence of safety; report uncertainty and obtain the correct product information without approaching the hazard.
有些危险类别根本不要求图标。没有图形、标签缺失或产品不明，都不证明安全；应报告不确定性，并在不接近危险的前提下取得准确产品信息。

00:15:21.624 --> 00:15:36.888
A supplier label connects the product identifier, supplier, pictograms, signal word, hazard statements and precautionary statements. Danger and Warning are signal words; they do not replace the actual hazard description.
供应商标签关联产品标识、供应商、图标、警示词、危险说明及防范说明。Danger与Warning是警示词，不能替代实际危险描述。

00:15:36.888 --> 00:15:49.224
Check that the Safety Data Sheet matches the product. In its sixteen-section format, identification and hazards come first; the revision date helps you recognize which document you are using.
核对安全数据表与产品是否一致。其16节格式首先列身份与危险；修订日期帮助识别正在使用哪一份文件。

00:15:49.224 --> 00:16:05.976
For an exposure question, find first aid in section four. Release information is in section six, exposure controls in section eight and reactivity in section ten. Use the relevant information with specialist advice rather than guessing from a symbol.
暴露问题可查第4节急救；泄漏信息在第6节，暴露控制在第8节，反应性在第10节。应结合专业建议使用相关信息，不能只凭图标猜测。

00:16:05.976 --> 00:16:20.712
An SDS describes a product; it does not measure oxygen, concentration or all mixtures at this incident. Reading it from a safe place can improve the report but does not grant entry or permission to clean a spill.
SDS描述产品，却不会测出本次事件的氧浓度、物质浓度或所有混合物。在安全位置阅读可改善报告，但不授权进入或清理泄漏。

00:16:20.712 --> 00:16:34.752
In a mass-casualty incident, triage aims to sort patients rapidly so limited resources are directed according to urgency. It is a time-limited first pass inside incident command, not complete clinical care.
在多伤员事件中，检伤目的是快速分流，让有限资源按紧迫程度配置。它是事件指挥中的限时初筛，不是完整临床照护。

00:16:34.752 --> 00:16:47.592
START is an adult-oriented framework; JumpSTART adapts the approach for children. Use the exact version taught by the school and current service plan rather than blending algorithms from different posters.
START是成人导向框架；JumpSTART针对儿童作出调整。应使用学校教授及服务计划中的准确版本，不能混搭不同海报的算法。

00:16:47.592 --> 00:16:57.912
Color categories communicate a priority, not a guarantee of outcome or a permanent label. A patient can move to a different priority when new findings emerge.
颜色类别传达优先级，不保证结局，也不是永久标签。新发现出现时，患者可能需要改变优先级。

00:16:57.912 --> 00:17:12.096
The current cards use Minor in green, Delayed in yellow, Immediate in red and Deceased in black. Match the actual local label and tracking process. A color is useful only if the team shares its meaning.
现行卡片以绿色表示Minor、黄色表示Delayed、红色表示Immediate、黑色表示Deceased。应匹配准确本地标签及追踪流程。只有团队共同理解其意义，颜色才有用。

00:17:12.096 --> 00:17:26.976
Minor does not mean no injury, and Delayed does not mean no care. They describe lower priority relative to immediate threats during this sort. Arrange the designated review and treatment process rather than leaving those groups unattended.
Minor不等于没有损伤，Delayed不等于不需照护。它们表示本轮分流中相对即时威胁较低的优先级。应安排指定复评及治疗流程，不能让这些组无人照管。

00:17:26.976 --> 00:17:43.176
The pediatric chart sends walking children to Minor and then secondary triage. For a child who cannot walk because of developmental stage or disability, inability to walk alone is not a category; use the current tool and appropriate secondary assessment.
儿童卡把能行走的儿童送入Minor，再作二次检伤。因发育阶段或残障不能行走的儿童，不能只凭不能走就定级，应使用现行工具及适当二次评估。

00:17:43.176 --> 00:18:00.240
Deceased is the posted MCI tool’s label, not a new independent authority to pronounce death, abandon a patient or apply this algorithm to ordinary resuscitation. Categories, patient tracking and reassessment operate within the activated incident plan.
Deceased是张贴多伤员工具的标签，不是新增独立死亡宣告、放弃患者，或在普通复苏中使用此算法的权限。分类、患者追踪及复评都在已启动事件计划内进行。

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:14.928
The current adult card first asks about walking on command and absence of major injury. Do not make every walking person automatically safe. For a non-walker, assess breathing and the specified airway-positioning branch.
当前成人卡首先询问能否按指令行走且没有重大伤情。不能把每名能走的人自动当成安全。对不能行走者，应检查呼吸及卡片指定的摆正气道分支。

00:18:14.928 --> 00:18:31.344
If breathing remains absent after positioning, the card label is Deceased; if breathing starts, it is Immediate. This is the activated incident’s triage tool, not permission to replace ordinary resuscitation decisions outside that context.
摆正气道后仍无呼吸，卡片标签为Deceased；恢复呼吸则为Immediate。这是已启动事件中的检伤工具，不授权在该情境之外替代普通复苏决策。

00:18:31.344 --> 00:18:49.896
With breathing present, use respiratory rate, radial pulse and simple-command response. More than thirty breaths per minute, an absent radial pulse or inability to follow a simple command reaches Immediate. Exactly thirty does not cross the rate branch by itself.
已有呼吸时，按呼吸频率、桡动脉脉搏及简单指令反应检查。每分钟超过30次、桡动脉脉搏缺失，或不能遵从简单指令，均进入Immediate。恰好30次本身未跨过频率分支。

00:18:49.896 --> 00:19:04.968
Other patients following that pathway are Delayed. Keep the approved brief lifesaving actions within the triage role; do not turn the first pass into full treatment or import an older capillary-refill threshold into this radial-pulse card.
该路径其余患者为Delayed。应把获准的简短救命措施限制在检伤角色内；不能把初筛变成完整治疗，也不能把旧毛细血管再充盈阈值加进这张桡动脉卡。

00:19:04.968 --> 00:19:19.320
In the current child chart, a non-walking child without spontaneous breathing first receives airway positioning. If breathing begins, the category is Immediate. Do not put the pulse check ahead of this airway step.
当前儿童卡中，不能行走且无自主呼吸的儿童，首先接受摆正气道。若恢复呼吸，类别为Immediate。不能把脉搏检查放在这一步气道处理之前。

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:32.880
If apnea persists, assess a palpable pulse. No pulse in this branch leads to the chart’s Deceased label. If a pulse is present, the chart directs five rescue breaths using the taught technique.
若仍无呼吸，再检查可触及脉搏。该分支无脉搏时，进入卡片的Deceased标签；若有脉搏，按受教技术进行5次人工呼吸。

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:49.320
Reassess breathing after those breaths. If it resumes, select Immediate; if apnea continues, follow the Deceased branch. The order matters because a child with respiratory arrest can differ from an adult in the corresponding rapid-sort tool.
5次呼吸后重新检查。恢复自主呼吸则选Immediate；仍无呼吸则进入Deceased分支。顺序重要，因为对应快速分流工具中，儿童呼吸停顿与成人可能不同。

00:19:49.320 --> 00:20:03.552
These are MCI classification branches under the current incident plan and trained role. A label is not a stand-alone death pronouncement or a replacement for routine pediatric resuscitation outside the MCI process.
这些是在当前事件计划与受训角色下使用的多伤员分类分支。标签不是独立死亡宣告，也不能替代多伤员流程之外的常规儿科复苏。

00:20:03.552 --> 00:20:19.368
For the breathing pathway, a rate below fifteen or above forty-five per minute reaches Immediate. A rate of exactly fifteen or forty-five stays within the range and continues to the next branch; it does not by itself establish Delayed.
在已有呼吸的路径中，每分钟低于15或高于45次，进入Immediate。恰好15或45次仍在范围内，应继续下一分支；不能仅凭频率就定为Delayed。

00:20:19.368 --> 00:20:30.192
A breathing child without a palpable pulse reaches Immediate in the perfusion branch. Do not confuse that with the different apneic, no-pulse branch we just followed.
有呼吸但无可触及脉搏的儿童，在灌注分支进入Immediate。不能与刚才无呼吸、无脉搏的另一分支混淆。

00:20:30.192 --> 00:20:47.568
The current graphic uses AVPU: Alert, response to Voice, response to Pain, or Unresponsive. Alert, voice response or an appropriate pain response follows Delayed; an inappropriate pain response or unresponsiveness follows Immediate.
当前图使用AVPU：清醒、对声音有反应、对疼痛有反应、无反应。清醒、声音反应或适当疼痛反应进入Delayed；不适当疼痛反应或无反应进入Immediate。

00:20:47.568 --> 00:21:03.120
The graphic gives withdrawal as an example of an appropriate pain response and posturing as an inappropriate one. Use the trained assessment; do not substitute a full GCS or classify a normally non-walking child by mobility alone.
图中把回缩作为适当疼痛反应示例，把异常姿势作为不适当反应示例。应采用受训评估，不能换成完整GCS，也不能只凭行动能力给本来就不会走路的儿童分类。

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:13.752
A quiet patient can deteriorate, and a patient initially classified as delayed can become immediate. Reassess at the interval and triggers in the current local plan.
安静的患者也可能恶化；最初列为延迟的患者可能变为立即处理。应按现行当地计划的间隔及触发条件复评。

00:21:13.752 --> 00:21:22.680
Use a clear tag and tracking process so that triage category, patient movement, treatment and transport assignment remain connected.
使用清楚的标记与追踪流程，确保检伤级别、患者移动、治疗及转运任务保持对应。

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:34.296
Secondary triage and clinical treatment occur in designated areas under command. Do not allow a self-selected destination or ad hoc transport to defeat the coordinated plan.
二次检伤及临床治疗应在指挥安排的区域进行。不能让自行选择的去向或临时转运破坏协调计划。

00:21:34.296 --> 00:21:48.936
In an original rehearsal at a cleared shelter walkway, Adult A cannot walk but breathes twenty-eight times per minute, has a radial pulse and follows a simple command. On the adult card, that pathway reaches Delayed.
在已确认安全的避难所通道原创演练中，成人A不能行走，但呼吸每分钟28次、有桡动脉脉搏，能遵从简单指令。成人卡的这一路径到达Delayed。

00:21:48.936 --> 00:22:02.400
Adult B breathes thirty-one times per minute. The rate already reaches Immediate. A child breathing forty-six times per minute also reaches Immediate, but through the pediatric rate boundary, not the adult number.
成人B呼吸每分钟31次，频率已达到Immediate。呼吸每分钟46次的儿童也达到Immediate，但依据儿童频率边界，不是成人数字。

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:16.944
Later Adult A stops following simple commands. Repeat the relevant assessment, identify the new Immediate concern and update the tag and treatment team through the incident process. The original label is not permanent.
之后成人A不再能遵从简单指令。应重复相关评估，识别新的Immediate问题，并通过事件流程更新标记及治疗团队。原有标签不是永久的。

00:22:16.944 --> 00:22:30.096
A useful update preserves patient identity, the changed finding and time, and the requested response. Do not remove the old timeline or send an untracked patient toward a self-selected ambulance.
有效更新保留患者身份、变化发现与时间，以及所需回应。不能抹去原时间线，也不能让未追踪患者走向自行选择的救护车。

00:22:30.096 --> 00:22:46.896
CBRNE stands for Chemical, Biological, Radiological, Nuclear and Explosive. A cluster of similar illness, unexplained odour, unusual residue, damaged containers or a scene inconsistent with the call can raise concern.
CBRNE代表化学、生物、放射性、核及爆炸危险。相似症状聚集、不明气味、异常残留、受损容器，或现场与报警内容不符，都可能提示风险。

00:22:46.896 --> 00:22:58.368
These clues are not a field diagnosis. Avoid touching, smelling closely, sampling or moving suspected material; relay observations from a safe position.
这些线索不能作为现场确诊依据。不要触碰、近距离嗅闻、取样或移动疑似物质；应在安全位置报告观察。

00:22:58.368 --> 00:23:09.984
A secondary device or continuing source may threaten responders after the first incident. Maintain distance, report the suspected hazard and await specialist direction.
首次事件后仍可能存在二次装置或持续暴露源，威胁救援人员。应保持距离、报告疑似危险并等待专业指令。

00:23:09.984 --> 00:23:21.168
Incident command and hazardous-material specialists define zones, access routes, decontamination and monitoring. Labels alone do not show that an area is safe.
事件指挥及危险品专家负责划定区域、通道、去污和监测；区域名称本身不能证明安全。

00:23:21.168 --> 00:23:31.248
Current BCEHS CBRNE guidance places clinical care in the cold zone. Medical awareness does not authorize routine entry into a hot or warm zone.
BCEHS现行CBRNE指导将临床照护置于冷区。具备医疗常识并不授权常规进入热区或温区。

00:23:31.248 --> 00:23:41.856
Do not enter to retrieve a patient, equipment or a partner without the required command authorization, specialist PPE, training and rescue capability.
未获得所需指挥授权、专业PPE、训练及救援能力时，不得进入危险区域取回患者、设备或同伴。

00:23:41.856 --> 00:23:57.096
Current BCEHS PR05 requires CliniCall contact with a paramedic specialist before assessing patients from a hazardous-material or chemical-exposure incident. Ordinary BCEHS equipment does not authorize work in the hot or warm zone.
现行BCEHS PR05要求，在评估危险品或化学暴露事件患者前，联系CliniCall救护专员。普通BCEHS装备不授权在热区或温区工作。

00:23:57.096 --> 00:24:14.760
Under the controlled plan, safe evacuation and clothing removal reduce ongoing exposure and secondary contamination. Explain the process, preserve dignity, arrange assistance for those who cannot follow instructions and control removed contaminated items.
在受控计划下，安全撤离及移除衣物可减少持续暴露与二次污染。应解释流程、保护尊严、为不能自行遵从者安排协助，并控制移除的污染物品。

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:33.696
The school’s blanket no-soap statement differs from PR05, which includes mild soap for wet decontamination. Do not infer that every unknown agent should simply be flooded with water; the dry or wet method is contaminant- and plan-dependent. Avoid abrasive scrubbing.
学校一概“不能用肥皂”的说法不同于PR05，后者在湿式去污中包括温和肥皂。不能据此推断所有未知物都应直接大量冲水；干式或湿式取决于污染物及计划。避免磨擦性刷洗。

00:24:33.696 --> 00:24:53.304
The CBRNE guidance prioritizes lifesaving airway and hemorrhage care over waiting for perfect decontamination, within safe roles and protection. This does not remove zone boundaries. Coordinate care, prevent hypothermia and notify receiving services about contamination risk.
CBRNE指导要求在安全角色与防护内，优先处理救命气道及大出血，而非等待完美去污。这不取消区域边界。应协调照护、防低体温，并通知接收机构污染风险。

00:24:53.304 --> 00:25:07.488
A freight truck has overturned at a rural intersection. Several people are injured, a cargo drum is damaged, and the contents are not yet known. A responder sees vapour near the truck but has not entered the area.
一辆货运卡车在乡间路口侧翻，多人受伤，一个货桶受损，内容物不明。救援人员在卡车附近看到蒸气，但尚未进入该区域。

00:25:07.488 --> 00:25:20.856
Before anyone approaches, the wind shifts toward the initial staging point. The team withdraws to the new safe side, warns crews already moving in and reports the changed hazard and access route.
在任何人接近之前，风向转向最初集结点。团队撤至新的安全侧，警告正在接近的救援组，并报告危险及通道变化。

00:25:20.856 --> 00:25:35.136
Command requests specialist hazardous-material support, confirms zone controls, and assigns a triage leader once a safe casualty area is established. The medical crew does not cross into an uncontrolled zone.
指挥请求危险品专业支援，确认区域控制，并在安全伤员区建立后指定检伤负责人。医疗组不会跨入未控制区域。

00:25:35.136 --> 00:25:46.776
A learning review asks what was expected, what actually happened, what changed, and what the team should keep or improve. It is focused on systems and decisions rather than blame.
学习复盘关注原本预期、实际发生、变化点及团队应保留或改进之处；重点是系统与决策，不是归罪。

00:25:46.776 --> 00:25:57.000
Protect patient and staff privacy in notes and discussion. Share only what is needed for handover, safety learning or the authorized reporting process.
记录及讨论中应保护患者和工作人员隐私；只分享交接、安全学习或授权报告所需的信息。

00:25:57.000 --> 00:26:08.688
The module’s scenario and reflection sections need active practice. A narrated lesson cannot demonstrate scene command, PPE competency or safe triage performance for you.
模块的情景与复盘章节需要主动练习。配音课程不能替你展示现场指挥、PPE能力或安全检伤表现。

00:26:08.688 --> 00:26:23.280
Experience helps only when you test whether the present scene is actually similar to the last one. Emotional urgency, a familiar address or a loud casualty can pull attention away from an unseen hazard or quieter patient.
只有检验当前现场是否真的像上一次，经验才有帮助。情绪紧迫、熟悉地址或声音大的伤员，都可能把注意力从隐患或安静患者身上拉走。

00:26:23.280 --> 00:26:39.240
In the review, name the cue you missed, the decision it affected and a practical repair. For example, a change report was transmitted but not acknowledged; the repair is a closed-loop update, not simply telling everyone to be more careful.
复盘时指出漏掉的线索、受影响的决定及实际改进。例如变化报告已发出却未获确认，改进是闭环更新，而不只是叫大家更小心。

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:56.880
Check readiness after a difficult incident. If concentration, emotional control or safe task performance is affected, tell the appropriate lead and use the available peer, supervisor or professional support pathway. You do not need to diagnose yourself to ask for help.
困难事件后应检查履职准备。若专注、情绪调节或安全执行任务受影响，应告知适当负责人，并使用同伴、主管或专业支持路径。请求帮助不需要先自行确诊。

00:26:56.880 --> 00:27:11.160
Keep operational learning specific and protect privacy. Restore equipment and supplies, record authorized follow-up and make the agreed change visible before the next call rather than treating the debrief as the end of the work.
行动学习要具体，并保护隐私。应恢复设备与物资、记录获准随访，并在下一次出车前落实约定改进，而非把复盘当成工作终点。
